A data-holder class whose fields are set and read only by callers
(oRecord:sOrderNo from another script), never inside the class file.
unused_variable (strict, hint) reports class-level :DECLARE names that the
file never mentions again; a class field is a member reachable from other
files, so single-file analysis cannot see its uses.
-- input.ssl --
/*
 * Class: OrderRecord
 * Description: Plain holder for order header values set by callers
;
:CLASS OrderRecord;
:DECLARE sOrderNo, dPlaced, nLineCount;

/*
 * Procedure: IsEmpty
 * Returns: .T. when no order number has been set
;
:PROCEDURE IsEmpty;
	:RETURN Empty(Me:sOrderNo);
:ENDPROC;
-- format --
/*
 * Class: OrderRecord
 * Description: Plain holder for order header values set by callers
;
:CLASS OrderRecord;
:DECLARE sOrderNo, dPlaced, nLineCount;

/*
 * Procedure: IsEmpty
 * Returns: .T. when no order number has been set
;
:PROCEDURE IsEmpty;
	:RETURN Empty(Me:sOrderNo);
:ENDPROC;
